From 0593c19c8b378ea991775bed045ac2095131c669 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:42:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gate): add the light tier for the heavy tests

`cargo xtask gate light` runs the light twins of the heavy tests in
release: one release build of the crates that hold a twin, then one
step for each test target with a twin. A twin has the ignore reason
`light lane: ...` and the name `<full test>_light`; the planner refuses
a twin whose file has no #[ignore]d full test. A red run prints the
note for the PR: each red step with the command of its full heavy step.

The first twin is the slot sweep of machining2d::adaptive (2 of its 20
rows). The full sweep does not change.

AGENTS.md names the light lane and the local full rerun after a red
cut gate. The text for the gate and release-cut skills is owed: the
worker session could not write in .claude/skills/.

Process change: yes

Refs #2569

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
